        "answer": {
          "short": "Missing entries, left to right in each row (including the header row):\nRow 1: $-3,-4$.\nRow 2: $-5,15,20$.\nRow 3: $4,8$.\nRow 4: $-6,-9$.",
          "worked": "Find the missing factors by dividing known products by their known factors:\n$$\\begin{align*}6\\div(-2)&=-3\\\\(-12)\\div3&=-4\\\\10\\div(-2)&=-5\\end{align*}$$\nFor each remaining product, determine the sign, then multiply the magnitudes:\n$$\\begin{align*}(-5)\\times(-3)&=15\\\\(-5)\\times(-4)&=20\\\\(-2)\\times(-2)&=4\\\\(-2)\\times(-4)&=8\\\\3\\times(-2)&=-6\\\\3\\times(-3)&=-9\\end{align*}$$",
